  "body": "## Summary\n\nCloses #3.\n\nAdds Codex CLI as a real dashboard data source when local Codex state is present.\n\n- reads Codex thread metadata from `~/.codex/state_5.sqlite`\n- reads token metrics from the latest cumulative `total_token_usage` object in each referenced rollout JSONL file\n- normalizes Codex records into overview totals, source cards, model breakdown, daily chart, and usage history\n- keeps OpenCode-only behavior unchanged when Codex data is missing\n- shows unavailable Codex cache-write metrics as unavailable instead of zero\n- documents the Codex source contract and trustworthy metrics in the README\n\n## Validation\n\n- `scripts/review.sh`\n- `uv run python -m unittest tests.test_app tests.test_readme -v`\n- `uv run python -m py_compile app.py scripts/snapshot_dashboard.py`\n- local API smoke against `PORT=8322 uv run python app.py`:\n  - `/api/overview?days=30` returned active OpenCode + active Codex + planned Hermes sources\n  - `/api/models?days=30` returned Codex model rows\n  - `/api/daily?days=30&top_n=5&tool_id=codex` returned Codex chart data\n  - `/api/usage-history?limit=50` returned recent rows including Codex entries\n- browser smoke on the local dashboard:\n  - Codex source card rendered as active\n  - model table showed Codex rows\n  - clicking Codex filtered the chart to Codex and preserved chart focus copy\n  - no console errors\n",
